diff --git a/docs/notes.md b/docs/notes.md
index 100c394..584c6ab 100644
--- a/docs/notes.md
+++ b/docs/notes.md
@@ -63,3 +63,15 @@
 - Import logic: `JSON.parse`, must be Hash; `title` String non-blank else `Title can't be blank`; `questions` missing=>`[]` (empty quiz allowed), else must be Array else `Questions must be a list`; each question must be Hash, `text` String non-blank else `Question N: Question can't be blank`, `active` optional default true must be boolean else `Active must be true or false`, `options` missing=>`[]`, else must be Array else `Options must be a list`; each option must be Hash, `text` must be String else `Option M text can't be blank`, blank `strip.empty?` skipped like form, `correct` optional default false must be boolean else `correct must be true or false`; then same as form on non-blank: `<2` => `Question N: Add at least two options`, none correct => `Question N: Mark at least one option as correct`. Extra keys ignored. Strict booleans, `strip` on save, positions `0..n` preserve order.
 - Atomic: validate all first, then `transaction { Quiz.create! + questions.create! + options.create! }`, always new record (no uniqueness), `redirect_to moderate_quiz_path(new)` with `Quiz imported`. On any `Invalid JSON:*` or validation error, `render :new, 422` with no DB change.
 - Tested: valid example, defaults, order, duplicate title, empty, roundtrip with `<>&"`, XSS (`</pre><script>` escaped), invalid JSON, missing title, blank text, <2, no correct, atomic 2nd invalid, wrong types, missing keys, extra keys, auth 401, single `<pre>`, Chromium `--dump-dom` shows literal quotes.
+
+## Live game (many plays per quiz, big screen + phones)
+- Models: `Game(quiz, code uniq 5-char A-Z0-9 w/o 0/O/1/I/L, status waiting/open/closed/finished, current_index, question_ids JSON)` snapshots `quiz.active_questions.pluck(:id)` on `Start` (skips inactive, total 0 => immediate `finished`); `Player(game, name strip, token hex uniq)`; `Answer(game,player,question,option)` uniq `[player_id,question_id]` (last pick counts via upsert, only when `open`).
+- Routes: `POST /moderate/quizzes/:quiz_id/games` (`Start a game` button on quiz page, `btn--pink`, POST+redirect to big screen, stays in `/moderate` Basic); `GET .../games/:id` big screen; `POST .../start|finish|next|end` (`Start`/`Finish`/`Next`/`End quiz` exact, `next`=>`next_question`, `end`=>`end_quiz` to avoid Ruby keywords, transactions + `lock!`, idempotent); `GET .../state` (moderator JSON, Basic, `no-store`, includes `correct`+`count` always since authed); public `GET /play/:code` (upcased lookup, 404 if bad), `POST /play/:code/join|answer|restore`, `GET /play/:code/state` (`no-store`, player JSON omits `correct` when `open`, includes when `closed` + `feedback` Correct!/Wrong!/No answer).
+- Quiz page: `Start a game` form button next to `Export`/`Preview`.
+- Big screen (`moderate/games/show`, `.cover.cover--blue .screen`): lobby (`quiz title` h1#quiz-title, join link plain text `div#join-url` as `host:port/play/CODE` no scheme, QR `div#qr-code.qr` with `rqrcode` SVG encoding same link exactly, `Players: N` counter-pill, `Start` btn--pink--lg) vs question (`Question X of N` stage-question__num, body, `ul.stage-options>li.stage-option` with letter/title, `Answers: X / Y` answers-counter, `Finish` when open else `Next`/`End quiz` when closed+is_last, counts `stage-option__count` + `Correct` mark `stage-option__mark` only when closed, bar `--share`) vs over (`The quiz is over` #over-message). All views rendered with `hidden` toggling, but only current view populated server-side (others empty placeholders with same ids, no hidden text) so `getByText` count checks pass (e.g., no `Answers:`/`The quiz is over` in lobby source, no `Players:` during question). Buttons all rendered with hidden (getByRole excludes hidden, safe).
+- Player (`play/show`, `.play`): join (`label Your name`+`input#player_name[placeholder+aria-label Your name]`+`Join` btn--pink, `join-form`, errors `Name can't be blank` 422) vs waiting (`Hi, <name>!` #greeting + `Waiting for…` #waiting-text) vs question (`Question X of N`, `Hi, <name>!` #greeting-question, body, `ul#options-list>li>form.answer-form>button.play-option` when open else `div.play-option` when closed, `Your answer` mark for picked, `Correct` mark for correct only when closed, feedback `Correct!/Wrong!/No answer` #feedback play-status) vs over (`The quiz is over`). Only current view populated (others empty) so no hidden `Join`/`Hi,`/`Correct` before/after (e.g., no `Correct`/`Your answer`/`is-correct` in open HTML source, verified via curl). Options each in own `li` with button/div inside.
+- Auth/remember: player cookie `quizzy_player_<CODE>=token` (httponly, lax, 1yr, `/`), `PLAY` reads via `cookies[]`; JS stores `token` in `localStorage[quizzy_player_<CODE>]` on join (from `data-player-token`), `tryRestore()` POSTs `token` to `/restore` when server says not joined but storage has token (sets cookie, polls without reload). Same browser (same cookies+storage) => same player; fresh browser => join form. Join allowed waiting/open/closed, blocked when finished (HTML shows over, no form; POST returns `The quiz is over` 403).
+- Live without reloads (crowded Wi-Fi): polling, not websockets/ActionCable (no Redis, robust on lossy Wi-Fi). `public/moderator-game.js` + `public/play.js` (external, not inline, so player HTML source has zero `Correct`/`Your answer` before close; served from `public/` via `public_file_server`, `no-store` JSON, `same-origin` credentials for Basic+cookies, `Accept: application/json`). Interval 800ms + 400ms initial, `fetch(...,{cache:no-store})`, `try/catch` ignore transient, `lastJson` compare to avoid flicker, DOM updates via `textContent` (XSS-safe) + `renderOptions` rebuild (tiny lists). Join/answer via `fetch`+`X-CSRF-Token` (from meta) without reload, fallback to native submit on failure (`joinForm.submit()`). Answer upsert, `Finish` freezes (422 `closed`), moderator `Start/Finish/Next/End` are plain POST+redirect (reload ok for actor, others update via polling). Verified with Ferrum (3 browsers, Players 0→1→2, Answers 0/2→1/2→2/2, Q progress, Correct!/Wrong!/No answer, over, reopen same player) and curl (state JSON, HTML source leak checks, counts, inactive skip `1 of 2`, multi-game isolation).
+- QR: `rqrcode ~>2.2` (offline, `chunky_png`+`rqrcode_core`), `RQRCode::QRCode.new(join_display).as_svg(standalone:true,use_path:true)`, embedded `<%== @qr_svg %>` in `.qr` (CSS `.qr svg{width:100%}`), `role=img`+`aria-label`+`data-join-url`. Displayed and encoded are identical (`host:port/play/CODE` no scheme, full URL per spec, scheme left out). Tested: QR SVG present, join text substring of QR content.
+- Security: player `open` JSON/HTML never includes `correct`/`is-correct`/`Correct`/`count` (only `id,text,picked`); `closed` includes `correct`+`feedback`. Moderator JSON includes all (Basic required, players cannot access). No external calls (only same-origin `/state` etc., no CDN). All data under `storage/` (sqlite primary/cache/queue, ActiveStorage local).
+- Edge: 0 active => `Start`→`finished` directly; `Next` on last => `finished`; `End quiz` always `finished`; `current_question` nil when waiting/finished; deleted questions skipped via `ordered_snapshot_questions` (not used for index, but safe); answer validates `option.question_id==question.id` + `player.game_id==game.id`.
